"{\"body\":\"T46 records audit, child of #693 / records epic #1415, M6.P2. Local actual primary Codex/GPT\u002d6\u002dAstra/xhigh, T3 wN:p6; one model perspective, reviewers[], no provider call or independent reviewer. Governing v2 647a8831739ffa28995e1955e68225ca0226c926; dispatch #693 comment6603284080.\\n\\n## Executive summary\\n\\n\\nOne Low Documentation Gap, L\u002d01 / PL\u002d001: current docs/audits/README.md:19 tells an audit reader to use `applyTo`, contrary to the named canonical `paths:` rule convention. Source remains unchanged. All95 direct targets resolve by immutable metadata;99 finite reading records retain exact ranges and masks. New controls pass their expected outcomes. This is a Stage\u002dD disposition packet, not final acceptance or an integrated\u002dnext claim.\\n\\nreviewed\u002dat: d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a\\nexecution\u002dseed: 8710a6210a40de0110244d03a886161ee06faf29\\nfixed\u002dat:\\n\\n## Acceptance\u002dcriteria scorecard\\n\\n| Brief criteria | Evidence / state at D |\\n| \u002d\u002d\u002d | \u002d\u002d\u002d |\\n| 1\u20134 source/identity/populations | 00\u201307, stage\u002da source\u002dbinding, table.json;127469 paths/2190843187 logical bytes,10 exhaustive roots; source distinct from seed |\\n| 5\u20136 finite readings | 95 keyed routes/89 targets,10 entrypoints,99 reading records;71 selected timestamp sections/15 unknown fallbacks; exact masks/unread status |\\n| 7\u20138 questions/ownership | Q1\u2013Q7 below,02 trace/self\u002drefutation, accepted T39 outcomes and #1407 boundary retained |\\n| 9\u201311 new controls/identity | Complete table positive+8 refusals, link controls, per\u002dcommit fixtures, namespaced actual Local plan+real lint fixtures |\\n| 12\u201314 D records/gates | Actual pre\u002dissue/issue/check receipts and readbacks in stage\u002dd; completion is claimed only when recorded there |\\n| 12 resolution half,15\u201318 final obligations | Await root disposition, later E\u2013H/acceptance/marker/integration; not selected or credited at D |\\n\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n\u002d [ ] PL\u002d001: the audit README\u2019s rule\u002dselector guidance agrees with the canonical paths/every\u002dsession convention, demonstrated by bounded source trace and current rules/record checks, with historical receipts unchanged; reactive bug #1416. Remains Open pending root stream disposition.\\n\\nAlready written: the documentary finding wrote no device/cloud state; no user\u002ddata migration is implicated.\\n\\nCan this be done on the VM? This immutable documentary/metadata analysis and new host record\u002dtool validation need no runtime. No device behavior is claimed; later runtime/removal proof requires a separate owning brief.\\n\\n## Punch list and retained evidence\\n\\n# T46 punch list \u2014 one Low item, disposition pending\\n\\n## PL\u002d001 \u2014 Current audit README names the obsolete rule key\\n\\nSeverity: Low. Category: Documentation Gap. Source finding L\u002d01. Question Q2 (also Q1/Q3/Q7). Owner area records.\\n\\nAt reviewed\u002dat d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a, docs/audits/README.md:19 says the instruction files whose `applyTo` matches changed paths define the rubric. The canonical .claude/rules/instruction\u002dfiles.md:9,27,37\u201347 defines `paths:` plus the no\u002dkey/every\u002dsession behavior. The surrounding README is current instructions, not a preserved command example.\\n\\nConsequence: an auditor following the literal key can select the wrong instructions or omit applicable ones. Self\u002drefutation: the canonical guide remains reachable, limiting severity; historical #314 methodology explains provenance but does not govern current rules. T39\u2019s retained46 outcome routes and bounded issue searches assign no existing correction for this key. Source unchanged; no Phase7 outcome chosen.\\n\\nAlready written: documentation has not written device/cloud state; no user\u002ddata migration is implicated. Historical receipts and author identities must remain byte\u002dexact.\\n\\nCan this be done on the VM? Documentary source comparison and current rule checks need no runtime; no device fact or guest behavior is claimed.\\n\\nAcceptance: a separately authorized current\u002ddoc correction names the actual `paths:` convention and every\u002dsession behavior, with a bounded source trace and rules/record checks showing the wording agrees with instruction\u002dfiles.md. Exact changed\u002dpath evidence must show historical receipts untouched. Root owns that stream disposition; this audit does not apply the correction.\\n\\nEvidence: 02\u002dforward\u002daudit.md L\u002d01, stage\u002db/table.json finding_trace, stage\u002db/read\u002d00/stdout, stage\u002db/inherited\u002dand\u002dduplicates.json. Reactive issue assigned in Stage D summary/readback.\\n\\n## Machine index\\n\\n```yaml\\npunch_index:\\n  \u002d id: PL\u002d001\\n    severity: Low\\n    category: Documentation Gap\\n    source_finding: L\u002d01\\n    question: Q2\\n    owner_area: records\\n    where: docs/audits/README.md:19\\n    acceptance: Current instruction names paths and every\u002dsession behavior with bounded source and rule\u002dcheck evidence; historical receipts unchanged.\\n    outcome: open\\n```\\n\\n## Phase 7 resolution gate\\n\\n| Item | Outcome | Evidence |\\n| \u002d\u002d\u002d | \u002d\u002d\u002d | \u002d\u002d\u002d |\\n| PL\u002d001 | Open | Stage D finding only; awaiting root stream disposition. No correction, deferral or withdrawal selected. |\\n\\n## Pre\u002dexisting tracked scope\\n\\nT39 accepted48 paths/15 Resolved/22 Deferred/9 Withdrawn remain owned by #686/#807/#346 for integration. #1407 retains monthly indexing and33\u002ddocument/2770\u002dline review under D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d223/224. No duplicate PL numbers or new resolution is assigned to those owners.\\n\\nPre\u002dissue lint PASS is retained at docs/audits/2026_11_03\u002depic\u002dm6\u002drecords/stage\u002dd/pre\u002dissue\u002dlint/receipt.json. New table/link/per\u002dcommit confinement controls have expected positive/refusal exits; stage\u002dc/control\u002dsummary.json lists all18 actual invocations. Exact source, range, mask and ownership tables are in stage\u002db/table.json. Publication checkpoint follows on #693; no E\u2013H, resolution, completion marker, acceptance, integration or closure is claimed.\",\"comments\":[],\"number\":1417,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"M6.P2: Audit: T46 records \u2014 1 finding (0 critical, 0 high)\"}\n"
